As she stitched, the cloak grew warm with the memory of every kindness she had ever offered. It glowed softly, lit by a memory of forgiveness she once refused to grant herself. The star warned that whoever wore the cloak could glimpse the truth behind every mask—both in others and in themselves. Asha, curious and compassionate, wrapped the cloak around her shoulders instead.

